{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500963-they-re-made-of-charms-spirit-creation-rules","id":1500963,"title":"They're Made of Charms! Spirit Creation Rules","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-01-21T14:30:40-08:00","id":1500963,"title":"They're Made of Charms! Spirit Creation Rules","content":"A little less then seven years ago I stumbled across <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/exalted-theyre-made-of-charms.470567/\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a> on RPG.net, detailing a system that represents the base 'chassis' of spirits through a set of Charms that define their Attributes, base Abilities, even their physical shape and capacity for personality. I found these rules really fun, and so over the course of several years I've picked away at converting them to work with 3e's ruleset. Somewhere along the way I decided to try and convert 2e's Spirit Charms from Roll of Glorious Divinity into 3e's ruleset as well, ballooning the size of this project immensely. I've had this done and sitting in my files for a few years now, and I decided to celebrate the return of the Onyx Path Forums by posting them here! So, without further ado, here's my conversion of They're Made of Charms! <div align=\"center\"><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Je7P1Z0bVZsKd9ynhLfITAYuIndpXCnViUuLNq25-Pc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><b><i><span style=\"font-size:22px\">They're Made of Charms!</span></i></b></a></div> <br /> <br /> Also, if anyone is interested, I created some <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1AUpKO7MP0HBqC74iin-NXdTUheaUb-XgaRMBco9jimw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">templates for gods of different celestial ranks</a>, based on the statblocks from 2e. I'm not sure if any of these rules are actually good or useful, but I figured that if I posted them somewhere and got some eyes on them they might eventually evolve into something generally useful for Storytellers and players alike. And who knows? Maybe at some point they'll be robust enough that I can finally use them to fulfill my fantasy of playing in an Exalted game as a Second Circle Demon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11619-kymmetheseventh","name":"KymmetheSeventh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-21T20:13:29-08:00","id":1500998,"title":"","content":"Hm... I'm not against the reintroduction of Virtues for Spirits, but you probably need some kind of guidelines how many virtue dots a Spirit should have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>---------------------------------------------<br /> Supporter of Spirits getting full playable splat design come Exalted 3E.<br /> Refugee from the 3rd Great Edition Wars of D&amp;D. <br /> oWoD Latecomer, Exalted Optimist, Scion ST, Trinity Curious","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/955-yue-ryong","name":"Yue Ryong","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar955_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"147"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-21T21:27:19-08:00","id":1501009,"title":"","content":"I think the original rules in 2e were something like.... Spirits start with Essence+5 dots to distribute among their Virtues, and then start with a Willpower equal to the sum of their two highest Virtues.<br /> <br /> As for why I included Virtues... I was mostly just sort of reluctant to take them out of the mechanics of They're Made of Charms without having anything with which to replace them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11619-kymmetheseventh","name":"KymmetheSeventh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-22T11:04:12-08:00","id":1501041,"title":"","content":"I'd stick to the new Willpower rules for Ex3 - start at 5, raise with points (mostly xp).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>---------------------------------------------<br /> Supporter of Spirits getting full playable splat design come Exalted 3E.<br /> Refugee from the 3rd Great Edition Wars of D&amp;D. <br /> oWoD Latecomer, Exalted Optimist, Scion ST, Trinity Curious","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/955-yue-ryong","name":"Yue Ryong","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar955_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"147"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T23:46:12-08:00","id":1502483,"title":"","content":"To allocate their Essence and an additional five dots among their Virtues, Spirits in 2e had a base Willpower equal to the sum of their two highest Virtues.<br /> <a href=\"https://run3online.io\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#ffffff\">run 3</span></a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27673-manisla","name":"Manisla","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"ke